---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getReferencesByIds, legalReferenceIds } from '../data/referenceRegistry';

const legalReferences = getReferencesByIds(legalReferenceIds);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Educational Disclaimer"
  description="The educational, examination, clinical, affiliation, accuracy, and external-service limitations of Komadrona Review."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal and educational limits</span>
      <h1>Educational disclaimer</h1>
      <p>Read this page before relying on any review article, practice question, score, or external link.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="container prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <strong>Not medical or clinical advice</strong>
      <p>
        Komadrona Review is an educational study resource. It is not a clinical protocol, patient-specific advice,
        professional consultation, or a substitute for supervised education and clinical training.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Independent and unofficial</h2>
    <p>
      Komadrona Review is independently created and maintained. It is not affiliated with, commissioned by, reviewed
      by, approved by, sponsored by, or endorsed by the Professional Regulation Commission, the Professional
      Regulatory Board of Midwifery, the Department of Health, the Commission on Higher Education, any educational
      institution, or any review center.
    </p>
    <p>
      References to agencies, laws, examination programs, and publications identify sources only. No agency seal,
      school seal, or official branding should be interpreted as part of this project.
    </p>

    <h2>No examination guarantee</h2>
    <p>
      The project does not guarantee that its material is complete, that any topic will appear in a licensure
      examination, that a learner is eligible to take an examination, or that use of the site will produce a passing
      score. Examination coverage, schedules, application requirements, and instructions may change.
    </p>
    <p>
      Users must verify current examination information directly through official PRC publications and announcements.
      The linked April 2026 examination program is used to structure the current Version 1 review map only and is not
      represented as a permanent Table of Specifications.
    </p>

    <h2>Original practice questions only</h2>
    <p>
      Practice questions are intended to be original educational exercises derived from official concepts and
      traceable references. They are not represented as actual, leaked, recalled, reconstructed, predicted, or
      officially endorsed licensure-examination questions.
    </p>
    <p>
      Submissions containing confidential examinations, commercial reviewer scans, faculty test banks, copied
      question sets, or instructions for obtaining restricted examination content will not be accepted.
    </p>

    <h2>Copyright and permitted use</h2>
    <p>
      Educational purpose does not create unlimited permission to copy protected material. Komadrona Review will write
      explanations and practice items originally, use limited quotations only when necessary, attribute sources, and
      link to official publications rather than rehosting full books, diagrams, tables, or question banks without clear
      permission or a compatible license.
    </p>

    <h2>Accuracy and changing guidance</h2>
    <p>
      Reasonable efforts will be made to identify sources, versions, review statuses, and correction dates.
      Nevertheless, laws, regulations, clinical guidance, examination programs, and accepted terminology can change.
      Errors or outdated statements may remain temporarily despite review.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where a site summary differs from a current official document, the current official document controls. For
      patient care or clinical decisions, follow applicable institutional protocols, current Philippine guidance, and
      qualified professional supervision.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy and local progress</h2>
    <p>
      Version 1 does not operate user accounts or a server-side learner database. Browser progress is local to the
      device and may be lost when site data is cleared or when the user changes browsers or devices. Hosting providers,
      external quiz services, and voluntary email communication may still process technical or identifying information
      under their own systems and policies.
    </p>

    <h2>External services</h2>
    <p>
      Practice activities may open through Google Forms or another clearly identified external service. Komadrona
      Review does not control the availability, interface, security, grading behavior, or privacy practices of that
      external service. Its own terms and privacy notice apply after the user leaves this website.
    </p>

    <h2>Funding and donation features</h2>
    <p>
      The initial release does not include a donation button, Maya QR code, visible wallet details, payment link,
      advertising, or sponsorship facility. Any later public-funding feature requires a separate review of applicable
      solicitation, hosting, privacy, accounting, and disclosure requirements before implementation.
    </p>

    <h2>Use at your own judgment</h2>
    <p>
      Users remain responsible for evaluating the material, consulting current primary sources, and deciding how to
      use the site. Nothing on Komadrona Review creates a professional, instructional, fiduciary, clinical, or legal
      relationship between the maintainer and the user.
    </p>

    <h2>Official references supporting this disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      These sources explain the examination framework, non-affiliation position, examination-integrity rule, privacy
      approach, copyright boundary, quiz configuration, and current exclusion of public donation features. Their
      inclusion does not mean any issuing body reviewed or approved Komadrona Review.
    </p>

    <ul class="source-list">
      {legalReferences.map((reference) => (
        <li>
          <div class="badge-row" style="margin: 0 0 0.75rem;">
            <span class="badge">{reference.priority}</span>
            <span class="badge">{reference.year}</span>
          </div>
          <strong>{reference.title}</strong>
          <span>{reference.issuer}</span>
          <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">{reference.use}</p>
          <a href={reference.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open official source</a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <p class="small-print">Last reviewed: 3 August 2026. This page is project disclosure, not legal advice.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
